    thinking: "**Building the Blog Section**\n\nI\'ve just finished the ProfileSection; it\'s looking great! Now I\'m shifting focus to `BlogSection.tsx`. I need to figure out the right structure to accommodate a tech blog, a Kannada blog, and more to come.\n\n\n**Designing the Blog Section**\n\nI\'ve hit a breakthrough! I\'m envisioning a unified, filterable blog browser that\'s incredibly usable. Each category \342\200\223 tech, Kannada, travel \342\200\223 will have distinct styling. The tech blog will use a structured essay style. Kannada will be rendered with beautiful Kannada typography and English sub-annotations. Travel posts will include card summaries, geographic tags, and modular maps. This is truly brilliant.\n\n\n**Refining the Blog Layout**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual details. The blog browser will present a stunning layout of responsive column cards, each showcasing the post title, category, date, reading time, and location details for travel posts. When a post is clicked, it transforms into an elegant reading view with a large title, header info, and a content block with custom formatting and high typographic contrast. The travel post details will be visually displayed using latitude and longitude coordinates, elevation (as a badge), and district/region. Kannada posts will feature beautiful Kannada titles and clean verse spacers, with an optional English summary. It\'s time to build `BlogSection.tsx`, potentially bypassing external markdown libraries!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `BlogSection.tsx` component, which orchestrates the Tech Blog, Kannada Blog, and Travel Blog interfaces. It supports clean tab selection, instant searching, tag filters, geographic elevation displays for travel locations, translation assists for Kannada articles, and an immersive single-post reading mode."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 746491664
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
