        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: \"tech-agentic-ui\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    type: \"tech\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    title: \"Beyond the Chatbox: Orchestrating the Dynamic Conversational Canvas\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    subtitle: \"Why the infinite scrolling bubble UI is a transition state, and how we build state-rich canvas layers.\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    date: \"2026-05-15\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    readingTime: \"8 min read\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    category: \"AI Systems\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    tags: [\"State Machines\", \"UX Paradigm\", \"AI Orchestration\"],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    intro: \"Most developers treat AI integration as a glorified chat logs box. But absolute UX mastery requires a shift: from appending raw string tokens inside a bubble layout, to updating a state-rich interactive canvas using schema-driven visual state-machines.\","
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    content: `### The Chat Balloon Fallacy"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "When LLMs went mainstream, we default-configured them to stream markdown text inside a scrolling container. It felt organic, like human chatting. However, as an engineering tool, this paradigm is deeply flawed:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. **Zero State Persistence:** Reading lines of text is ephemeral. If the model mentions a \'new database configuration\', it shouldn\'t just print YAML; it should update a structural database widget live on screen."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. **High Cognitive Overhead:** The screen scrolls continuously, pushing important, actionable items out of viewport bounds."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. **Weak Constraints:** Raw strings have no visual bounds. Handing an AI full freedom to write random HTML often crashes rendering queues."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### The State-Rich Canvas Architecture"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "To transition toward genuine **Agentic Interfaces**, we define a state-rich architectural model. The layout is divided into a **Control Stream** and an **Active State Canvas**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "\\`\\`\\`"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "   [ Prompt Input ] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [ LLM Planner Engine ] "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
