    thinking: "**Designing the Personal Card**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a personal card within the `ProfileSection.tsx` file. I\'m exploring different naming conventions for this card. I\'m considering \"The Builder\'s Tension Map\" or \"Personal Operational Axioms\" to best capture its purpose.\n\n\n**Defining Foundational Struggles**\n\nI\'m now thinking about an interactive, tabbed state-view within the personal card. This will feature three toggles representing foundational struggles: Velocity vs. Rigor, AI Agents vs. Guaranteed Logic, and Sovereign Space vs. Guild Exchange. Each toggle will include a styled sliding scale and a personal developer\'s note, along with a \"Structural Bylaw\" or \"Personal Principle\". This card\'s design aims to be intensely personal.\n\n\n**Refining Digital Sketchbook Visuals**\n\nI\'m now striving for a curated \"Digital Sketchbook of an Architect\'s Core Tensions\" look, steering clear of enterprise software aesthetics. The state design for the personal card is planned, with states like `\'rigor\'`, `\'intelligence\'`, and `\'focus\'`. Currently, I\'m fleshing out the \'rigor\' state, which includes a slider biased toward rigor, a narrative, and a by-law statement. I\'m focusing on the balance between conceptual rigor and practical velocity. I am also currently working on the other state representations.\n\n\n**Analyzing AI Applications**\n\nI\'ve just added AI agent application narratives to the \"Personal Operational Axioms\" card. I\'ve defined a slider rating focused on deterministic models versus fuzzy heuristics, with a narrative emphasizing high-assurance relational assertions around AI outputs. The \"AI\" state will also contain a metric I\'m calling \"RULE_02\".\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Prioritizing Focus Metrics**\n\nI\'m now detailing a \"focus\" state within the card, framing the tension as solitary deep craft versus community node. This state will include a slider rating of focused solitude versus community sharing, alongside a narrative about the balance between deep work and external connection, and a by-law concept.\n\n\n"
